{
 "name": "Phase-field Bubbles 6: lava lamp (many)",
 "description": "A lava lamp of many bubbles, big, medium and small, each starting at its own temperature. Warm ones rise, cool ones sink; the heater along the bottom warms any bubble there and the cooler along the top cools it, and a bubble keeps its temperature in between, so each rises all the way, cools, sinks all the way and warms again. They bump rather than merge. Tint shows temperature. Slow, so bubbles keep their content and shape: raise steps per frame if your GPU keeps up. Work in progress: small dots bud off in the heater and cooler (20 bubbles become about 45 islands by 400k steps).",
